  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing the harmful consequences of conflicts on FSL in Sa&apos;ada</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The specific objective of the project is &quot;Promoting resilience and protection of crisis - affected communities by strengthening their self -protection capacities, responding to and advocating on protection risks, and reducing their food insecurity through survivors -centred and community -led approaches&quot;. This will be achieved through three interconnected outcomes that feed into each other.  Outcome 1 envisages providing protection services through the community -based protection centres and referrals to other service providers by linkages development, and supporting persons with protection risks with accessing legal/civil documentation. Communities&apos; capacities in self -protection will be improved through capacity -strengthening of community -based protection networks, enabling a cadre of youth from local communities to work at the community -based protection centres and acquire skills and knowledge, and implementing community -based local initiatives through protection grants with the support of CBPN and community members. The project will also focus on conducting protection monitoring, analysis and reporting, and disseminating analysis reports to influence practices and policies. Outcome 2 envisages building resilience capacities of vulnerable communities by forming self -help groups (SHGs) and capacitating them in disaster preparedness and response, undertaking a capacity and vulnerability analysis. SHGs will be  supported to formulate  community -based disaster preparedness and response plans, combined with provision of cash grants to communities/SHGs for preparedness/response. Extremely vulnerable HHs at high protection risks (also referred through community centres) will receive MPCA to meet their immediate food/non -food needs during the first month of a disaster. Likewise, resilience, coping capacities, and self -sufficiency of households and communities will be improved to reduce protection risks associated with their livelihoods strategies through supporting Income Gene</narrative>
  </description>
